================================================================================
CHALLENGE 6: THE ANY-TYPE LOGGER (GENERIC CONSTRUCTORS)
================================================================================
1. THE CLASS:
   - Create a normal class `LogEntry` (NO <T> on the class name itself).
   - Add a private String field `message`.

2. THE CONSTRUCTOR:
   - Create a constructor with its own type parameter:
     `public <T> LogEntry(T data)`
   - Logic: `this.message = "LOG [" + data.getClass().getSimpleName() + "]: " + data;`

3. THE TEST:
   - Create one LogEntry with a `String`, one with `Double`, and one with `Boolean`.
   - Print the `message` of each.
   - This proves that constructors can be generic even if the class is not!
================================================================================